# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Tauri generates these from tauri.conf.json and the capability files at build time.
crates/dile-app/gen/
src-tauri/gen/

# Node and any built frontend
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never commit an updater private key. Losing it means never shipping an update to the
# installed base again; leaking it means someone else can.
*.key
*.pem
minisign*.key

# Local machine state
*.log
.env
.env.*
# Agent and editor working state: the whole directory, not just the local settings file,
# so a wide `git add` can never sweep a machine-specific config into a commit.
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Models and audio never live in this repository (docs/PROJECT.md §3 Distribution, §4).
# Weights and benchmark material live outside the repository; the app downloads weights from
# Hugging Face at run time.
models/
*.bin
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.wav
*.mp4

# One exception, and it is not a recording: WP3's probe clip is two seconds of Windows' own
# Turkish text-to-speech voice reading a neutral sentence. 64 KB, compiled into the binary,
# because the first-run GPU probe has to be the same audio on every machine. The command
# that regenerates it is in docs/BUILDING.md.
!crates/dile-app/assets/probe.wav

# The sidecars, copied into the name Tauri's `externalBin` expects by
# `scripts/build-host.ps1`. Build artefacts like everything else in `target/`, and committing
# a binary to satisfy a build step is how a repository ends up shipping a stale one.
crates/dile-app/binaries/
